+## 3. Decisions and rationale
+1. **S-2: one guard, `pipeline.js#pauseError`.**
+   - It applies to `company.paused` or `crawlBlock(source, board)`, so a custom spelling of a paused built-in's
+     board is refused too.
+   - Callers: `fetchLive`, `snapshot.js one()` (before the crawl state is read, so both fetch paths are covered)
+     and the probe's full mode, which calls adapters directly.
+   - The 2026-10-11 S-2 tests assumed Amazon and Meta were paused. They now set `paused` on registry entries for
+     their run, so they test the guard instead of today's registry.
+   - The probe already skipped paused slugs. Its gap was Google's careers hosts: they lacked `www.google.com`,
+     the adapter's origin, so raw mode could still reach a paused Google.
+2. **S-4: posting hosts per company, in the registry entries** (`postingHosts`, `postingPrefixes`).
+   - A first version put the table in `server/sources/links.js`. The stable build then shipped it in
+     `dist/lib/` (normalize.js imports it), and `test/beta-build.test.js` failed: a beta host on the main site.
+   - In the entries, the stable site's `lib/companies.js` (beta entries removed by `stableRegistry`) ships none.
+   - `postingRule` looks the rule up by slug, so a caller's partial copy still gets it.
+   - `scripts/links-policy.js` builds the same two lists from the entries; a test pins them to the old literals.
+   - normalize.js names no host, not even in comments, because it ships on the stable site.
+   - Amazon keeps `job_path` verbatim when the joined URL is on-origin, so real links are byte-identical
+     (22,179 of 22,179).
+3. **S-4 drawer.** `applyHost` returns '' for anything but an absolute http(s) link. The foot then shows
+   `p.muted` "No link to the posting" (inline flex style, no CSS change) instead of the Apply link. The Copy-link
+   button stays.
+4. **S-10.**
+   - Bounds as the lead specified: amounts trimmed and cut to 100 characters; titles cut to 500 with
+     `[（(][^（(）)]{0,200}[）)]`; `<loc>[^<]{0,2048}</loc>`; the JSON-LD type attribute within 500 characters
+     of `<script`.
+   - The JSON-LD reader's trailing `[^>]*>` and body `[\s\S]*?</script>` were also quadratic, so a bound alone
+     was not enough. It is now a forward scan with cached next-`>` and next-type positions and a last-`</script>`
+     index. It is exact except for the 500-character bound.
+   - The DOL regexes (`CELL_RE`, the rich-text pair, `<rPh>`) are forward scans with the same results; seeded
+     fuzz of 5,000 cell strings agrees.
+   - The bracket rule differs from the old one only for nested brackets. 0 of the 37,619 real titles nest, and
+     `familyOfTitle` is unchanged on all of them.
+5. **V14.**
+   - `customBoardName` suffixes " (custom)", the suffix `public/app.js#companyInfo` already gives the header.
+   - Names are compared loosely (NFKC, case, spaces, punctuation), so "A.P.P.L.E" and "scale ai" are caught.
+   - `defaultName` uses it too, so the cached copy's name never collides.
+   - On the stable static site the browser registry holds stable entries only, so beta names are guarded in
+     server mode and on /beta/, and stable names everywhere.
+6. **V12.**
+   - persist-credentials: false on every checkout except the four jobs that push with the checkout token
+     (archive-ingest ×2, persist-ledger ×2, all `contents: write`). The test now walks every workflow.
+   - The tap is fetched at a pinned commit, with no brew auto-update. The pip install uses
+     `--require-hashes --only-binary :all:` against `.github/scripts/idb-requirements.txt`.
+   - `pip download` for macOS arm64 / cp314 resolves exactly the 8 packages of run 38979700118.
+7. **S-9 residual.**
+   - A Node checker, `.github/scripts/fx-values-only.mjs`, from the tip's `.github/`, which the allow-list keeps
+     the refresh away from.
+   - It masks the values the FX writer changes and requires each code copy to equal the tip otherwise. That is
+     stricter than a line-shape check: a valid-looking row added elsewhere, or a key added, is also refused.
+   - It accepts `FX_AS_OF`, `FX_SOURCE`, `EXTRA_FX_PER_USD` and the `FX_FALLBACK` CNY rate as well as the rows,
+     because `9de373f` changed all of them.
+   - The `9de373f` replay uses its hunks with 8 lines of context: CI checks out at depth 1, so it has no history.
+8. **S-9, test code: no FX example to move.**
+   - `test/juice.test.js` holds no pinned FX example. Its Big Mac date pin was already made relational, and the
+     `TEST_PINS` rule that names the file is detect-only.
+   - It was on the allow-list only because the allow-list test read every `file:` literal, detect rules
+     included. README.md and docs/CONTRACT.md were there for the same reason.
+   - All three are removed. The allow-list test now reads the writers' `{ file, content }` write sites and
+     checks that no test file and no code besides the four FX copies is listed.
+   - So no `test/fixtures/fx-examples.json` was made: nothing would read or write it.
